  "equipment_type": "Networked room thermostat",
  "applies_to": "Daikin light commercial rooftop units and heat pumps controlled by the BACnet AppStat thermostat.",
  "summary": "The Daikin AppStat is a programmable BACnet thermostat for light commercial rooftop units and heat pumps. It joins a BACnet MS/TP trunk (the PICS ticks MS/TP master only) and exposes about 70 objects: sensor inputs, staging outputs, setpoint and configuration AVs, status BVs, occupancy/system/fan mode MSVs and three PID loop objects. Several instances change meaning between rooftop and heat pump configurations.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Application APP0.0.1.1, firmware R1.0.0.15 (PICS)",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "BO 2-4, AV 13 and AV 19 mean different things on rooftop and heat pump units; both names are shown.",
    "Object names follow the guide's 'Full Reference' names (e.g. Act_Cool_Stpt); points with no full reference keep the keypad name from the table (e.g. MIN_STPT_DIFF, FAN_SPEED).",
    "Fan_Mode (MV 3) states are 0=Auto, 1=ON in the table but 1=Auto, 2=Low/ON, 3=Medium, 4=High in the detail section; check on the device.",
    "BV 15 Rev_Vlv_Polarity is only in the detailed point section, not the summary table; access is not stated.",
    "The thermostat also has a BACnet schedule object for network scheduling; its instance is not listed.",
    "The guide's intro mentions BACnet/IP, but the PICS and setup table only cover MS/TP."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet Design Guide - BACnet Thermostat Protocol Information (Table 5: BACnet Standard Objects)",
    "doc_number": "DG-DAPPS",
    "revision_date": "10/19",
    "url": "https://daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/appstat--bacnet-thermostat/dg-dapps.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set Device ID, MAC address and baud on the thermostat's Communication menu (level 2 password); it resets after each change. The BMS then commands Occupied_Mode and System_Mode, writes the occupied setpoints and reads space temperature, discharge air temperature, heat/cool mode and fan proof. The internal schedule is a BACnet schedule object that a workstation can edit.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "MV 1",
        "name": "Occupied_Mode",
        "why": "Occupancy command: occupied, standby, unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 2",
        "name": "System_Mode",
        "why": "System mode: off, auto, cool, heat"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 3",
        "name": "Fan_Mode",
        "why": "Fan mode command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 5",
        "name": "Occ_Cl_Stpt",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 6",
        "name": "Occ_Ht_Stpt",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 1",
        "name": "Fan",
        "why": "Fan start/stop output (1 = on)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 8",
        "name": "Mode",
        "why": "Current heat or cool mode"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "Space_Temp",
        "why": "Space temperature used for control"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 20",
        "name": "Discharge_Temp",
        "why": "Discharge air temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 14",
        "name": "Fan_Status",
        "why": "Fan proof alarm (0 = alarm)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "There is no separate enable point. Occupied_Mode (MV 1), System_Mode (MV 2) and Fan_Mode (MV 3) are commandable and act directly; Occ_Schedule (BV 5) reflects the schedule. Local overrides from the keypad show in Local_Ovrd (BV 28) and Stpt_Hold (BV 36).",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Device ID, MS/TP MAC address (1-127) and baud (Auto, 9600, 19200, 38400 or 76800) are set in the keypad Communication menu; a level 2 password is needed.",
      "With a MicroTech integrated system use device instances 3101001-3101127 and 38400 baud.",
      "The thermostat cycles power and resets after any communication setting change.",
      "Default device object name for MS/TP is BAC-######## (from production number and date code)."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "BO 2-4, AV 13 and AV 19 change meaning between rooftop and heat pump setups.",
      "Speed_Up_Cl (BV 11) shortens all timers by 15x; use it for start-up and service only.",
      "Fan_Mode states differ between the table and the detail section; confirm on the device."
    ]
  },
